<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilbert Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a> Islands are a chain of sixteen coral atolls in the central Pacific, inhabited by Micronesian I-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiribati">Kiribati</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over them in 1892, joined them with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellice-islands">Ellice Islands</a> as a colony, and they became the core of independent Kiribati in 1979. The atoll kingdom of Abemama lay in the central group.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gilbert-islands.jpg" alt="Gilbert Islands" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pitichinaccio · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GilbertIslandsPos.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
